  "question": {
    "text": "The number of roots of the equation <math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>LHS is always non negative.<br />So, RHS also has to be the same</p><p>So, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math><br />Squaring both sides, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>as</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
}